  "details": "Description\n\nWhen I unplugged my headphones from my Quest 3, all vrc audio stopped. I can still have the audio run through my pc, but there's nothing going through my headset. I am hearing the menu sounds when I open my Oculus settings, so I know it isn't my headset. I tried to plug my headphones back into my Quest, but there is still no audio. I checked all of my audio settings in vrc and muted & unmuted all of the audios, and nothing worked.\n\nReproduction Steps\n\nI am unsure how to recreate this bug. As far as a workaround, you can use the headphone jacks on your pc until the issue is resolved\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: Audio\n\n- Frequency: Once\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.4.2-1953-d52354d5be-Release\n\nunityVersion: 6000.0.67f1-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report",
